content:
Powerhouse provides the `OID` (Object ID) custom scalar type for unique identifiers in document models. Key patterns:

- Objects in arrays must have an `id: OID!` field
- IDs are non-deterministic, so they must be generated **before `dispatch`** with `generateId()` and passed in through the action input — never generated inside the reducer
- `AddTodoItemInput` therefore carries `id: OID!` alongside `text`, and the reducer reads `action.input.id`
- Update and delete operations require `id: OID!` to identify the target

```typescript
// In the editor - generate the ID before dispatching
import { generateId } from "document-model";

dispatch(addTodoItem({ id: generateId(), text: input.text }));
```

```typescript
// In the reducer - read the ID from the input
addTodoItemOperation(state, action) {
  state.items.push({ id: action.input.id, text: action.input.text, checked: false });
}
```

`generateId()` is `crypto.randomUUID()` under the hood, so calling it inside a reducer breaks replay determinism — two peers replaying the same operation log would produce different IDs. Generating at the dispatch site gives you unique, consistent IDs *and* a reducer that stays a pure function of `(state, action)`.

_Corrected 2026-08-13 against Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45._
